.TH "kreastrap.kg" "5" "" "" ""
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
kreastrap.kg - declarative Kongue configuration for
\f[V]krep rootfs\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Rootfs configurations are declarative Kongue documents stored as
\f[V]share/krep/rootfs/arch/ARCH/configs/BUILD_TYPE.kg\f[R].
The loader accepts only literal scalar and list fields: functions,
commands, interpolation, mutation, qualifiers, duplicate fields, and
unknown fields are rejected.
.PP
Only \f[V].kg\f[R] Kongue rootfs configurations are supported.
.SH EXAMPLE
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
schema_version: \[dq]1\[dq]
build_directory: \[dq]/out\[dq]
package_mode: \[dq]binary\[dq]
use_overlay: \[dq]true\[dq]

arch: \[dq]x86_64\[dq]
os: \[dq]linux\[dq]
libc: \[dq]glibc\[dq]
compiler: \[dq]gcc\[dq]
coreutils: \[dq]gnu\[dq]
init: \[dq]systemd\[dq]
tls_library: \[dq]openssl\[dq]

extra_packages:
  - \[dq]gmake\[dq]
  - \[dq]nim\[dq]
\f[R]
.fi
.SH FIELDS
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[V]schema_version\f[R]: Schema version; currently \f[V]1\f[R].
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[V]build_directory\f[R]: Rootfs output directory.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[V]package_mode\f[R]: \f[V]binary\f[R] to consume published archives
or \f[V]build\f[R] to build.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[V]use_overlay\f[R]: Whether to copy the selected rootfs overlay.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[V]arch\f[R]: Canonical package architecture, such as \f[V]x86_64\f[R]
or \f[V]aarch64\f[R].
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[V]os\f[R]: Target OS; currently \f[V]linux\f[R].
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[V]libc\f[R]: \f[V]glibc\f[R] or \f[V]musl\f[R].
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[V]compiler\f[R]: \f[V]gcc\f[R], \f[V]clang\f[R], or \f[V]no\f[R].
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[V]coreutils\f[R]: \f[V]busybox\f[R] or \f[V]gnu\f[R].
GNU membership is defined by the repository group \f[V]gnu-core\f[R],
not by this configuration.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[V]init\f[R]: \f[V]busybox\f[R], \f[V]jumpstart\f[R],
\f[V]openrc\f[R], \f[V]runit\f[R], or \f[V]systemd\f[R].
Systemd profiles require GNU coreutils.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[V]tls_library\f[R]: TLS implementation, normally \f[V]openssl\f[R] or
\f[V]libressl\f[R].
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[V]package_roots\f[R]: Optional explicit resolved package roots.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[V]extra_packages\f[R]: Additional packages installed after core
profile roots.
.SH STATE
.PP
Provisioning writes \f[V]rootfs-state.kg\f[R] into the root.
It records the canonical profile, fingerprint, target, package roots,
phase, pending packages, and ready, deferred, provisioning, or failed
status.
The state is generated atomically; only
\f[V]status: \[dq]ready\[dq]\f[R] with
\f[V]phase: \[dq]complete\[dq]\f[R] is reusable.
